On **.NET 10+**, you no longer need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport`. Instead, configure `global.json`:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

That's it. With this setting, `dotnet test` talks directly to MTP — no bridge property needed, and arguments are passed directly (no `--` separator required).

**Key differences from .NET 9:**

| .NET 9 (old way) | .NET 10 (new way) |
|---|---|
| `<TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>true</TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>` in Directory.Build.props | `"test": { "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform" }` in global.json |
| Need `--` separator: `dotnet test -- --report-trx` | Direct: `dotnet test --report-trx` |

You still need the framework-specific runner enablement (`EnableMSTestRunner`, `EnableNUnitRunner`, etc.) and `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>` — those are unchanged. Want me to update your `global.json` and project files?
